stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    state "PROPOSED - intent raised, nothing changed for the person" as PROPOSED
    state "GATE_PENDING - waiting for a named confirmer, time and reason" as GATE
    state "SNAPSHOT_PENDING - composing the reconstruction payload" as SNAP
    state "COMMITTED - state change and decision record are durable together" as COMMITTED
    state "ABANDONED - lapsed or withdrawn before commit" as ABANDONED
    state "REVERSED - a later decision reversed this one" as REVERSED

    [*] --> PROPOSED: G1 decision intent, actor holds the decide permission
    PROPOSED --> COMMITTED: G2 not adverse, or influence is NONE
    PROPOSED --> GATE: G3 adverse and influence is not NONE
    GATE --> SNAP: G4 named natural person confirms with a non-empty reason
    GATE --> ABANDONED: G5 withdrawn, or the proposal ages out
    SNAP --> COMMITTED: G6 every required block present
    SNAP --> GATE: G7 composition failed, commit rolled back, FR-T-D017
    COMMITTED --> REVERSED: G8 a reversing decision passes the gate in its own right
    COMMITTED --> COMMITTED: G9 reason amended by the original confirmer, appended not edited
    ABANDONED --> [*]
    REVERSED --> [*]

    note right of GATE
        Refused as confirmer: service accounts, integration
        principals, shared logins, schedulers and the subject
        of the decision. A delegate is allowed where configured
        and is recorded as a delegate.
    end note

    note right of SNAP
        There is no configuration that commits an influenced
        adverse decision without a snapshot. A failure here
        leaves the person's state untouched.
    end note
